    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Let me summarize the implementation.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` field for owner creation. The value is `true` when more than 80 owners already exist on the new owner's registration date at create time, otherwise `false`, and it's persisted so `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns it (which is how the acceptance test reads it back).\n\nChanges, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (the same pattern used by `namesakeCount`/`customerCode`):\n\n1. **`AssignOwnerBulkSignupWarning.java`** (new function) \u2014 counts existing owners sharing the built owner's `registrationDate` and sets `bulkSignupWarning = count > 80`. Runs on the built `@Val Owner`, before persistence so only existing owners are counted.\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `bulkSignupWarning` step into the create pipeline between `namesakeCount` and `save`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`.\n\n3. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `bulkSignupWarning` (`Boolean`, `bulk_signup_warning` column) field with getter/setter.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct auto-maps it (matching property name \u2014 no explicit `@Mapping` needed).\n\n5. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added `bulk_signup_warning BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE` to the `owners` table.\n\nTest results: `AcceptanceTest` passes, and the full `./mvnw test` run is `BUILD SUCCESS` (1 test \u2014 the only one in the suite).",
