    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is structurally clean and, more importantly, it faithfully mirrors the existing `namesakeCount` feature that already lives in this codebase:\n\n- `AssignOwnerBulkSignupWarning` is a direct analogue of `AssignOwnerNamesakeCount` \u2014 a single-purpose function class with one public `service` method, in the correct `rest.function.owner` package, taking `@Val Owner` + `OwnerRepository` and mutating the entity in place per the OfficeFloor conventions in AGENTS.md. Logic sits in its own step, not bolted onto an existing catch-all.\n- The persisted `@Column` field + getter/setter on `Owner`, the parallel column additions across all four schema dialects, and the `readOnly` OpenAPI property all follow the exact pattern established by `namesakeCount`. A maintainer here would find nothing surprising.\n- The YAML wiring inserts the new step between `namesakeCount` and `save` with `govern: [ transaction ]`, consistent with the surrounding steps, and the Javadoc documents the ordering constraints (after `DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate`, before `SaveOwner`) that justify its placement.\n- DTOs stay at the edges; the intermediate step works on the entity. No duplication introduced \u2014 the same-date counting is distinct from the same-name counting in `AssignOwnerNamesakeCount`, so there's nothing to factor out.\n\nThe change is coherent, additive, and idiomatic for this repository. (I'm reviewing structure only, as instructed \u2014 I did not evaluate whether persisting a derived response flag or the `findAll()`-based counting is correct/efficient, only whether it fits the codebase's established shape, which it does.)",
